      "description": "Watch Sporting Charleroi II vs OH Leuven highlights and goals from Jupiler Pro League on ReFooty: Football Highlights Hub. Match played on August 10, 2026. The Jupiler Pro League delivered a high-octane encounter on August 10, 2026, as Sporting Charleroi II took on OH Leuven . It was a game marked by disciplinary flashpoints and moments of individual brilliance that kept the spectators on the edge of their seats. Early Penalties and Red Card Drama The match ignited in the 24th minute when Sporting Charleroi were awarded a penalty. Parfait Guiagon stepped up and coolly converted from the spot to put his side ahead. However, the momentum shifted just minutes later. In the 30th minute, Abdoul Karim Traore of OH Leuven was shown a straight red card following a heated incident, sparking heavy protests from his teammates. Despite being down to ten men, OH Leuven showed incredible resilience. In the 39th minute, Wouter George provided a pinpoint assist for Oscar Gil , who found the back of the net to level the score. The first half ended in a physical battle, with Chukwubuikem Ikwuemesi picking up a yellow card just before the break as the intensity reached boiling point. Charleroi Reclaim Control The second half saw Sporting Charleroi utilize their numerical advantage. After a half-time substitution that saw Isaac Cisse enter the fray, the home side intensified their pressure. In the 59th minute, Kevin Van Den Kerkhof restored the lead for Charleroi , finishing a well-worked move that left the OH Leuven defense scrambling. As the clock ticked down, both managers turned to their benches to find a spark. OH Leuven introduced fresh legs like Shin Yamada , but Charleroi remained clinical. In the 79th minute, substitute Freddy Mbemba made an immediate impact, scoring the third goal after a clever assist from Isaac Cisse . The referee blew the final whistle at 90+3', concluding a fixture defined by Traore’s dismissal and Charleroi’s second-half dominance."
